      "content": "The high-pitched staccato burst could be a confirmation signal, often referred to as a \"ACK\" (acknowledgment) or \"energy\" symbol in optical systems. This signal would typically follow the handshake to signal that the receiving device is ready to accept the data. The absence of encryption makes it less likely to be a secure communication channel, which rules out anything like SSL/TLS. A more likely scenario would be a regular Ethernet or Wi-Fi traffic packet being transmitted after the handshake.",
